Subject: [PATCH] controller: reconcile current associations without replaying history

Associated Clients reports include whole-second association ages. Do not let
an old AP claim overwrite a newer join, departure or association recovered
from another Agent. Keep disconnected Station history as the existing native
notification path does; prune only current ownership and detach erased global
stations from their BSS. Missing Associated Clients TLV means no associated
clients in the authoritative topology response.

Complete recovered associations through native connection handling, including
previous-AP cleanup and fresh metrics initialization. Unchanged membership
keeps timestamps and does not repeat connection work. Reject malformed or
foreign BSS entries before changing membership. Ambiguous ages (within the
one-second report quantization) do not override a newer recorded event; a
live association notification remains authoritative.

